---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, contactHref, href } from '../../lib/site';
const { standard, founding, foundingSeats, trialDays } = SITE.pricing;
---

<Page
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the BidRadar website, free sample and paid email digest."
  path="/terms/"
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="October 28, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to the BidRadar website, the free sample and the paid subscription
    (together, the "Service"). By signing up for the sample or subscribing, you agree to them. If
    you do not agree, please do not use the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What the Service is</h2>
  <p>
    BidRadar sends an email digest, on U.S. business days, of newly posted federal construction and
    facilities contract opportunities. Each item includes the notice title, agency, dates, a link to
    the original public notice, and BidRadar's own summary, 1-5 fit score and bid suggestion. The
    digest is filtered by the trades and states you tell us.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Independence from the government</h2>
  <p>
    BidRadar is an independent private service. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated
    by SAM.gov, the General Services Administration, or any U.S. government agency. Opportunity
    information comes from public notices. The original notice on SAM.gov, including any
    amendments, is the only authoritative source.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information only, no guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    Summaries, scores and suggestions are opinions to help you sort opportunities. They may be
    incomplete or contain mistakes, and notices can change after we write about them. We do not
    guarantee that the digest includes every relevant opportunity, that any information is
    accurate or current, or that you will win any contract. You are responsible for reading the
    full solicitation, confirming your eligibility, and every decision you make about bidding.
    BidRadar does not provide legal, financial or procurement advice.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Free sample</h2>
  <p>
    The free sample is {trialDays} weekday digests. No payment details are required. After the
    sample we may send one email asking whether you want to subscribe. You can unsubscribe at any
    time.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Subscription, price and billing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The standard price is ${standard} per month in U.S. dollars.</li>
    <li>
      Our first {foundingSeats} paying customers pay a founding rate of ${founding} per month. That
      price will not increase for as long as that subscription stays active.
    </li>
    <li>
      Subscriptions renew monthly until cancelled. Payments are processed by our payment provider,
      Creem, under its own terms. We do not receive or store your full card details.
    </li>
    <li>
      If we ever change the standard price, we will email existing subscribers at least 30 days
      before the change applies to them.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time by emailing <a href={contactHref}>{SITE.email}</a> or replying to any
    digest. Cancellation stops future billing. Your digest continues until the end of the period you
    have already paid for.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied during your first paid month, we will refund that month in full. See
    the <a href={href('/refund/')}>Refund Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    The digest is for your own business. Please do not resell it, republish it in bulk, or share
    your subscription with other companies. Forwarding an individual opportunity to a teaming
    partner is fine.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The summaries, scores, suggestions and the design of the digest and website belong to
    BidRadar. Notice titles, agency names and the notices themselves are public information.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to the Service or these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update the Service or these terms. If a change materially affects paid subscribers, we
    will tell you by email before it takes effect. Continuing to use the Service after that means
    you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, BidRadar is not liable for any indirect or consequential loss,
    including lost profits, lost contracts or bid costs, arising from use of the Service. Our total
    liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid us in the three months before the
    claim.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Ending the Service</h2>
  <p>
    We may suspend accounts that misuse the Service. If we ever stop operating BidRadar, we will
    tell subscribers by email and refund any unused paid period.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={contactHref}>{SITE.email}</a>, or by mail to {SITE.address.line1},
    {SITE.address.line2}, {SITE.address.line3}, {SITE.address.country}.
  </p>
</Page>
